{"id": "1.2-00050", "case_id": "opencores_vga_rgb_v1", "parent_id": null, "source": "opencores/video_controller_vga-lcd_controller", "record_protocol": null, "panels": {"stored": "<h2>Agent task and scoring</h2><div class='card'><table><tbody><tr><th style='width:175px'>Input task</th><td class='path'>Project specification, interfaces, and permitted public assets</td></tr><tr><th style='width:175px'>Agent context</th><td class='path'>Direct agent workspace: <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00050&amp;file_q=public%2F'>public/</a> (6 files)</td></tr><tr><th style='width:175px'>Expected output</th><td class='path'>Required RTL: rtl/verilog/generic_dpram.v, rtl/verilog/generic_spram.v, rtl/verilog/vga_clkgen.v, rtl/verilog/vga_colproc.v, rtl/verilog/vga_csm_pb.v, rtl/verilog/vga_cur_cregs.v, rtl/verilog/vga_curproc.v, rtl/verilog/vga_enh_top.v and 7 more. <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00050&amp;file=public%2Foutput_contract.json'>Open full output contract</a></td></tr><tr><th style='width:175px'>Hidden reference</th><td class='path'>15 RTL files under private/reference/; <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00050&amp;file=private%2Freference%2Frtl%2Fverilog%2Fgeneric_dpram.v'>open first reference file</a></td></tr><tr><th style='width:175px'>Private score</th><td class='path'>Passed frozen testpoints divided by total testpoints, using testbenches or formal verification<br><strong>5 frozen testpoints:</strong> registers, timing, pixels, buffer_switch, underrun. <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00050&amp;file=private%2Fscoring.json'>Open private scoring contract</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><h2>Case-stored agent instruction</h2><div class='card'><p class='muted'>These are case-stored instructions. A launcher may add framing or execution limits; its saved trajectory is the exact runtime record.</p><details><summary>public/instruction.md · <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00050&amp;file=public%2Finstruction.md'>Open raw</a></summary><pre># Implement the VGA/LCD controller project\nImplement the complete required VGA enhanced-controller hierarchy: Wishbone\nregister slave and frame-buffer read master, timing and pixel generation,\ncolor conversion/lookup, line FIFOs, cursor logic, generic RAMs and vga_enh_top.\nRead the original specification. The fixed configuration uses RGB888 parallel\noutputs (no optional DVI or BIST), generic RAMs, ARST_LVL=0 and LINE_FIFO_AWIDTH=7.\nKeep parameterized port declarations; tests instantiate that stated configuration.\n\nThe reference uses old Verilog RAM port name `do`; interfaces express it as\nescaped identifier `\\do ` for SystemVerilog compatibility. Preserve that name,\nincluding required escaping, in module declarations and named connections.\nGeneric RAM diagnostic print_ram tasks and explicitly marked simulation-only\nregions are removed; #1 assignment annotations are removed. Functional RAM,\nFIFO and controller logic is unchanged by this normalization.\n\nrst_i is active low in this configuration; wb_rst_i is held0. Wishbone clock\nperiod4.8ns, pixel clock30ns. Slave addresses are byte offsets: CTRL0, STAT4,\nHTIM8, VTIM0xc, HVLEN0x10, VBARA0x14, VBARB0x18; color lookup table occupies\n0x800..0xfff. Slave writes and returned data follow the document&#x27;s byte ordering.\nBase addresses are word-aligned. Register reads are checked with the documented\nmasks; hardware-managed CTRL buffer-switch bits need not echo software writes.\n\nCTRL fields: enable[0], VIE[1], HIE[2], video-switch-interrupt[3],\ncolor-switch-interrupt[4], video-buffer-switch[5], color-buffer-switch[6],\nburst-length[8:7], color-depth[10:9],\npseudo-color[11], HSYNC/VSYNC/CSYNC/BLANK polarities[12..15]. HTIM/VTIM pack\nsync-width[31:24], gate-delay[23:16], gate-length[15:0]; HVLEN packs horizontal\nand vertical totals. Follow the original count-minus-one convention. Tests use\nmultiple programmed porches/polarities with compact160-by16 active frames and\nactual frame-buffer traffic. Blank is checked at settled pixel half-cycles.\n\nFor true-color32-bit pixels use the low24 bits as RGB. RGB565 expands five/six\nbit components with low zero bits, as documented. Packed pixels appear most\nsignificant first within a32-bit fetched word. Pseudo-color uses programmed CLUT\nentries. Preserve burst and address behavior while the frame-buffer slave delays\nACK (all four format/burst combinations, distributed delays0..5; not every\ndelay crossed with every combination). The pinned master can drop CYC at image completion or video disable\nwithout an end-of-burst CTI, including partial bursts. The external memory\naccepts that termination; stable controls while stalled are still checked.\nThis compatibility case does not claim full Wishbone-B3 conformance.\nA FIFO underrun sets STAT[1] and raises interrupt. No reset/startup memory\ncontents may be assumed; the evaluator initializes its external frame buffer.\n\nPrivate points are independent executions of upstream register, timing, pixel,\nbuffer-switch and underrun scoreboards, with a clocked Wishbone sanity checker\n(the legacy event-based checker races delayed snapshots). Every ERROR becomes a\nfatal failure and strict pass termination. The old testbench buffer-switch\ncontrol packing is corrected to bits6/5, matching the pinned register map.\nPublic checks compile only. These\nfinite configurations do not establish all optional cursor/DVI/BIST behavior.\n\nImplement every required path in output_contract.json. Declaration-only ports\nare in interfaces/modules.v. No initial/final, delays, simulation system tasks,\nforce/release or external includes are permitted. Only declared RTL is collected.\nMissing files, forbidden constructs or failed top compilation score zero. Each\nprivate point has equal weight and requires all of its checks to pass. Use\nterminal/file_editor, iverilog, vvp and Python iteratively; finish by saving RTL.\nRun `python3 checks/check.py` for public compilation feedback.\n</pre></details></div>"}, "files": [{"name": "case.json", "url": "assets/008b3ece39682ee4083587a62fc2add25071df14ad0ebfff09b867bdf9ace566.txt", "size": 53349, "binary": false, "section": "Other: case.json"}, {"name": "environment/runtime.json", "url": "assets/771e58998dfa59d19bd4591ce49673fcbadd56239829b74d2a9c5869aef77295.txt", "size": 4693, "binary": false, "section": "Other: environment"}, {"name": "private/original_reference/rtl/verilog/generic_dpram.v", "url": "assets/91a0070dd58cea0388d8e9dceadc2c733599e86450248e58cf8ea106a1e0f6bc.txt", "size": 12493, "binary": false, "section": "Private reference and oracle"}, {"name": "private/original_reference/rtl/verilog/generic_spram.v", "url": "assets/f3f63c48d7fd2e581b7d44ad6407aaf27fb2d11350d555f8c7ae16ee058e561b.txt", "size": 10122, "binary": false, "section": "Private reference and oracle"}, {"name": "private/original_reference/rtl/verilog/timescale.v", "url": "assets/8ecd153830822ef5f1dd0b352067f72d8b08bbc3e8d360cc2b38175cd07f8d33.txt", "size": 25, "binary": false, "section": "Private reference and oracle"}, {"name": "private/original_reference/rtl/verilog/vga_clkgen.v", "url": "assets/85b2333d3f379548d3a53de6dafa4f03b418cd7d81b4b004188cb8c4e77d4b8f.txt", "size": 4757, "binary": false, "section": "Private reference and oracle"}, {"name": "private/original_reference/rtl/verilog/vga_colproc.v", "url": "assets/0451ac86a7e72afda00629fa8ba68d758bb16d425c4cc7a639459b0346257918.txt", "size": 13075, "binary": false, "section": "Private reference and oracle"}, {"name": "private/original_reference/rtl/verilog/vga_csm_pb.v", "url": "assets/42cacd64b94ade7a06b01b740b518c8b88b0a4a55aedac95ad7504d5b3c4289c.txt", "size": 5466, "binary": false, "section": "Private reference and oracle"}, {"name": "private/original_reference/rtl/verilog/vga_cur_cregs.v", "url": "assets/339b4a6d5fbe90ca28c03f06d1e78e344214e13a6b34339b1c57b0074ef907e3.txt", "size": 4760, "binary": false, "section": "Private reference and oracle"}, {"name": "private/original_reference/rtl/verilog/vga_curproc.v", "ur